    "statement": "Not pre-registered (added after the task review; the pre-registered verdicts stand as computed). The pre-registered mode A pair is r + j: the ghost inside r carries the recording's Bussgang gain beta = 1.0224 (the clean twin's mean Re(z / z_ref)), but the jammer added in mode A passes no quantiser, so normalising mode A by its own gain scales its jammer term by 1 / beta; in the real chain ghost and jammer both pass the quantiser. A3's variance ratio and P1's R(real/A) therefore carry a factor of about beta^2 = 1.045. Pre-registered / confound-free (the exploratory E2 structure, ghost and jammer both injected; mode A's gain 1.0007): variance ratio noise-60 1.246/1.186, swept_cw-60 1.171/1.126, noise-70 1.072/1.029, swept_cw-70 1.092/1.046; R(real/A) noise-60 1.062/1.014, swept_cw-60 1.018/0.994, noise-70 1.049/1.005, swept_cw-70 1.074/1.034; cancellation share noise-60 0.753/0.928, swept_cw-60 0.887/1.045, noise-70 0.304/0.820, swept_cw-70 0.188/0.261. In the confound-free construction A3's conditions still hold: noise variance ratio 1.186 (> 1.1), cancellation share 0.93 (>= 0.5); swept_cw variance ratio 1.126 (> 1.1), cancellation share 1.04 (>= 0.5); the truth's R(real/A) is 0.994-1.034. The same factor means mode A understates the jamming-induced error of satellites inside a 3-bit recording by about 4.3 % (1 / beta^2 - 1 = -0.0433); injected ghosts, added digitally like the jammer, carry no such factor."
